title: Public Spending
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/spending.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and public_spending_timer <= 0
on-arrival: public_spending_timer = 4; month_actions += 1

= Public Spending

The Chief Secretary's annual spending round. Every department wants more; the Treasury wants less. Spending is currently [+ spending : taxation +] compared with Labour's plans.

[? if cabinet_dry < 60 : The wets in Cabinet will fight any cut to their departments. ?]

- @cut: Cut spending.
- @deep_cuts: Deep cuts across Whitehall.
- @protect: Protect the NHS and pensions.
- @invest: Invest in roads, housing and job schemes.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@cut
view-if: spending > -5
subtitle: +2 budget.
on-arrival: spending -= 1; budget += 2; de_con -= 2; c2_con -= 1; wet_dissent += 4; cabinet_revolt += 1 if cabinet_dry < 60

Cash limits are tightened across the board. Councils, schools and hospitals feel the squeeze.

@deep_cuts
view-if: spending > -5
subtitle: +4 budget. Requires a dry Chancellor.
choose-if: chancellor_dry = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ chancellor +] won't propose cuts this deep.
on-arrival: spending -= 2; budget += 4; de_con -= 4; c2_con -= 2; c1_con -= 1; wet_dissent += 8; cabinet_revolt += 2 if cabinet_dry < 60; rebellion += 1

The Treasury demands cuts from every department. In Cabinet, the wets fight department by department.

@protect
view-if: spending < 5
subtitle: -1 budget.
on-arrival: spending += 1; budget -= 1; de_con += 2*(1-dissent); wet_dissent -= 3; dry_dissent += 2

"The NHS is safe in our hands." Pensions are protected too.

@invest
view-if: spending < 5
subtitle: -2 budget. Cuts unemployment.
on-arrival: spending += 1; budget -= 2; unemployment -= 0.4; economic_growth += 0.3; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); wet_dissent -= 4; dry_dissent += 4

New roads, council repairs and youth training schemes. Michael Heseltine is delighted. Sir Keith Joseph asks who will pay for it.
